    "overall_status": "partial_outage",
    "severity": "major",
    "suspected_causes": [
      "All 4 major ISP international gateways (TIC x2, Irancell, Asiatech) remain externally unreachable while BGP routes hold — sustained stealth blackout posture with centralized DPI + protocol whitelist at national gateway layer, consistent with Bock et al. FOCI'20 whitelister architecture",
      "Gateway failure-mode taxonomy now stable across observed passes: TIC GW 1 (2.187.1.1) + Irancell GW (5.232.0.1) both emit TCP RST ('connection refused'); TIC GW 2 (78.38.112.1) + Asiatech GW (94.182.0.1) both silent i/o timeout — two distinct suppression methods operating in parallel suggest DPI appliances configured per-node with either active RST injection or silent packet-drop modes",
      "Protocol whitelist enforcement stable at 4.2% — 45 of 1,068 labeled IP ranges reachable across 78 operators (down 1 from 46, within noise margin); UDP/ICMP/SSH/VPN silently dropped at gateway per IRBlock (Tai et al.) USENIX Security '25",
      "Electro DNS (78.157.42.100) persistently timing out while Shecan (178.22.122.100, 228ms) and TIC DNS (217.218.155.155, 228ms) remain operational — sustained targeted suppression of anti-censorship DNS resolver infrastructure",
      "Asiatech dual failure persists — gateway (94.182.0.1 timeout) + web portal (www.asiatech.ir deadline exceeded) both down — ISP-specific isolation likely under CRA directive or sustained infrastructure degradation",
      "Snapp (snapp.ir) remains in redirect-loop error state (stopped after 10 redirects) — unchanged across all observed passes; persistent DPI rule-state fluctuation or application-layer misconfiguration on NIN-routed traffic",
      "Shaparak payment gateway (www.shaparak.ir) deadline-exceeded timeout persists — domestic payment infrastructure degradation or targeted application-layer filtering at NIN layer",
      "Foreign platforms (Google, Telegram, Instagram, YouTube, WhatsApp, Wikipedia, GitHub, Cloudflare) all reachable from outside with low latency (59-443ms) — confirms filtering is directional (inbound to Iran blocked, outbound from Iran allowed) not BGP withdrawal",
      "Circumvention infrastructure (Tor Project, BridgeDB, Snowflake broker, Psiphon) all externally reachable — endpoints not themselves blocked, but protocol-level filtering at TIC gateways prevents Iranian users from establishing Tor/VPN tunnels regardless of endpoint availability"
    ],
    "affected_services": [
      "TIC gateways (2.187.1.1 connection refused, 78.38.112.1 timeout)",
      "Irancell gateway (5.232.0.1 connection refused — established pattern)",
      "Asiatech gateway (94.182.0.1 timeout) + web portal (www.asiatech.ir deadline exceeded)",
      "Electro DNS (78.157.42.100 timeout)",
      "Snapp (snapp.ir redirect loop, 10 redirects)",
      "Shaparak payment gateway (www.shaparak.ir timeout)",
